<title>UK: Memory makes fresh agreement with Sumitomo.</title>
<headline>Memory makes fresh agreement with Sumitomo.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memory Corp Plc said on Thursday that it has agreed with Japan's Sumitomo Corp to work together in selling Memory Corp technology in Japan and the Pacific Rim.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the agreement fits the company's strategy to sell differentiated technologies.</p>
<p>Both companies had a previous agreement dating back to the founding of Memory in 1993 in sourcing memory chips and selling completed Memory modules in the Asia market. That agreement ended in December 1996 by mutual consent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
